---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Not found | Coulter Heiberger"
  description="That page doesn't exist."
  eyebrow="Not found"
  noindex
>
  {/* NO CARVE-OUT FOR THIS ROUTE. lighthouserc.cjs's own header says there is
      "one bar across all URLs, with no relaxation for 404.html", and the same
      posture decides the layout: a route that opts out of the site's furniture
      is the first crack in "the staple is on every page". So /404 carries the
      Masthead, and it is the centring that gave way rather than the header —
      see the note in the style block. */}
  <h2>404</h2>
  <p>That page doesn't exist.</p>
  <p><a href="/">Back to the start</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Ground, ink, families and muted all come from tokens.css. This page used to
     declare its own — a pre-Datum :root block with hex literals for --bg/--fg/
     --muted plus font-family: ui-sans-serif — which issue #21 caught rendering a
     FOURTH family on a live page.

     Astro does not scope `:root`, so that block was emitted unscoped and
     overrode the derived --muted site-wide on this document, replacing a
     color-mix() with a hard-coded hex. That is the one thing docs/styling.md
     forbids outright: a component never hard-codes a value a token names, and
     never redefines a derived token. Nothing here paints a colour now. */

  /* THE CENTRING IS GONE, AND THAT IS WHAT MADE ROOM FOR THE MASTHEAD. This
     page used to set `display: grid; place-items: center; text-align: center`
     on <main>. Under a left-aligned Masthead that reads as two different pages
     stacked: the site's one datum edge is its name (see the long note on
     `/projects/<slug>/`), and a centred column under a header that starts at the
     gutter breaks it on the one route where nobody would think to look.

     So the header stayed and the centring went. There is no layout left to
     declare — the measure, the gutter and `flex: 1` all come from base.css's
     rule for the direct children of <body>, and `flex: 1` is still what puts the
     footer on the bottom of the viewport on a short page.

     THIS PAGE NOW OFFERS TWO WAYS OUT: the Masthead portrait's About band and
     the link below. That is a change to what a 404 is and it was a conscious
     yes, not a side effect.

     AND IT SCROLLS NOW, WHICH IS THE COST TO KNOW ABOUT. The note on `body` in
     base.css records that this page's own `min-height: 100dvh` was removed
     because "a 100dvh main plus a footer is one screen and a bit, which is a 404
     page you have to scroll" — and the Masthead has now done that anyway: 1092px
     at 1440x900, so the footer is ~190px below the fold. A face, a name, a lede
     and a specification line is most of a screen before the word 404 is reached.
     `flex: 1` still does its job; there is simply more than one screen to fill.
     ADR-0011 holds it as a known cost. */

  /* --t-h2, the same size a Project's title takes, because this is the same
     thing: the page's own heading. It used to be a third clamp and a third
     letter-spacing, both within a few hundredths of the shared pair and both
     invisible as a difference — a bespoke type size on the one page nobody
     designs.

     AN h2 FOR THE REASON A PROJECT'S TITLE IS ONE: the Masthead carries the
     site's name as the h1 on every route now, and tokens.css's rule is that h2
     is a page's own title. The size is unchanged. */
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--t-h2);
  }

  p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* The link sits inside a --muted paragraph, so without this it inherits
     --muted and is distinguished from the sentence around it only by a --rule
     underline — a 1.54:1 hairline. Lifting the link to --ink and giving the
     underline --muted (4.90:1) makes it the most contrasted thing on the page,
     which is right for the only action a 404 offers.

     A design fix, not gate compliance: axe fires link-in-text-block only when a
     link is distinguished from its surrounding text BY COLOUR, and this link
     was not distinguished at all, so the audit was notApplicable and CI was
     never going to force it. Issue #35. */
  a {
    color: var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
